1
00:00:02,214 --> 00:00:07,355
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,778 --> 00:00:09,859
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,751 --> 00:00:13,560
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:14,162 --> 00:00:19,265
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:20,212 --> 00:00:24,168
رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي َوَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي َوَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِنْ لِسَانِي َيَفْقَهُوا قَوْلِي

6
00:00:24,915 --> 00:00:31,709
During the time of Jahilliyah(جَاهلِيَّة), a man from Bannu Hadhrami(بنوالحزرمي), who was an ally of the Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر).

7
00:00:31,978 --> 00:00:35,018
You have sometimes, men who don't belong to a tribe,

8
00:00:35,694 --> 00:00:41,636
and they move and live with a certain tribe and then they become their allies.

9
00:00:42,148 --> 00:00:44,446
And what is meant by allies, is that,

10
00:00:44,906 --> 00:00:49,510
the tribe protects this person and takes care of them.

11
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:57,638
And they treat such a person as a member of their tribe in terms of protection that is offered by the tribe, to its members.

12
00:00:57,971 --> 00:01:02,257
So, this man from Bannu Hadhrami(بنوالحزرمي), he was traveling in Hijaz(حجاز),

13
00:01:02,402 --> 00:01:06,092
and when he was deep in the land of Khuza'a(خزاعه),

14
00:01:06,266 --> 00:01:08,314
Khuza'a(خزاعه) killed him, and stole his money.

15
00:01:08,518 --> 00:01:12,640
So, Khuza'a(خزاعه) have committed this crime against this man.

16
00:01:13,243 --> 00:01:15,424
And they killed him to take away his money.

17
00:01:16,025 --> 00:01:21,606
So, the people of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر), they took revenge by killing a member of Khuza'a(خزاعه)

18
00:01:21,938 --> 00:01:28,329
Khuza'a(خزاعه) then targeted three from the family of Bannu Aswad Ad-Doali(بنو الأسود أديلي)

19
00:01:29,028 --> 00:01:32,907
and Bannu Aswad(بنوالأسود) belong to the tribe of Bannu Bakr(بنو بكر).

20
00:01:33,122 --> 00:01:38,748
But they considered themselves to be above everyone else, and they consider themselves to be the noblest

21
00:01:39,204 --> 00:01:43,586
and they were considered to be the noblest among them.

22
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:46,789
In fact, they used to charge double the Diya(الدية),

23
00:01:47,459 --> 00:01:48,765
Diya(الدية) is the blood money.

24
00:01:48,990 --> 00:01:51,944
So, everybody else from Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) would take one Diya(الدية),

25
00:01:51,984 --> 00:01:58,951
while the children of Aswad(ألأسود) would take double the blood money.

26
00:01:59,423 --> 00:02:00,994
Khuza'a(خزاعه) killed three of them.

27
00:02:01,383 --> 00:02:08,034
And then Islam came and you would recall from Sulhal Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبية) that we said,

28
00:02:08,506 --> 00:02:14,322
one of the terms of the agreement is that whoever wants to enter into an alliance with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) can do so.

29
00:02:14,559 --> 00:02:18,651
And whoever wants to enter into an alliance with Muhammadﷺ can do so.

30
00:02:19,073 --> 00:02:22,917
So, Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) they entered into an alliance with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

31
00:02:23,179 --> 00:02:26,546
and Khuza'a(خزاعه) entered into an alliance with Muhammadﷺ

32
00:02:26,816 --> 00:02:30,133
Khuza'a(خزاعه) were allies of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم), in the time of Jahiliyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

33
00:02:30,434 --> 00:02:36,407
And now they became allies of the son and the leader of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم), Muhammadﷺ,

34
00:02:36,432 --> 00:02:39,136
even though many of them were Mushrik(مشرك) at that time.

35
00:02:39,632 --> 00:02:43,563
Some of Khuza'a(خزاعه) were Muslim and some of them were disbelievers.

36
00:02:43,684 --> 00:02:46,691
Nevertheless, they were all loyal to Muhammadﷺ

37
00:02:46,715 --> 00:02:50,403
even the disbelievers among them were loyal to Muhammadﷺ

38
00:02:50,646 --> 00:02:53,582
because of tribal tradition, not because of religion.

39
00:02:54,063 --> 00:02:57,616
They were the allies of Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) before Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة)

40
00:02:57,815 --> 00:03:04,083
and now they consider themselves to be allies of Muhammadﷺ, even though, they are Kuffar(كفار).

41
00:03:04,673 --> 00:03:09,388
Now, Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) they want to seek revenge for the three of them, that were killed

42
00:03:09,412 --> 00:03:12,970
and we're not talking about any three, we're talking about some noblemen among them.

43
00:03:13,412 --> 00:03:19,719
One of the leaders of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر), his name is Muawiyyah Bin Nofal Ad- Doali(معاويه بن نوفل ألديلي),

44
00:03:20,222 --> 00:03:22,419
he was one of their leaders, he wasn't the only leader.

45
00:03:23,063 --> 00:03:32,508
In tribal societies you have every small clan from the tribe has a Shaikh(شيخ) or Areef(عريف) or a leader, chief of the clan.

46
00:03:33,045 --> 00:03:37,450
So, Muawiyyah Bin Nofal Ad- Doali(معاويه بن نوفل ألديلي), who is from the branch of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر)

47
00:03:37,851 --> 00:03:43,039
that lost these three men, he attacked some people from Khuza'a(خزاعه)

48
00:03:43,063 --> 00:03:44,749
because I'm saying people, not men

49
00:03:44,789 --> 00:03:49,504
because in one narration it says that they were elderly and children and women.

50
00:03:50,258 --> 00:03:53,049
And these were as it says in the narration,

51
00:03:53,248 --> 00:03:55,593
بِجَوَارَهْ اَنْصَابْ عَرَفَاتْ

52
00:03:55,996 --> 00:03:57,914
They were next to the the Haram(حرم),

53
00:03:58,033 --> 00:04:03,706
the Haram(حرم) had stone marks to indicate, where the land of Haram(حرم) is.

54
00:04:03,919 --> 00:04:07,772
So, these were very close to those stone marks but they were outside of Al-Haram(الحرم).

55
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:11,004
Muawiyyah Bin Nofal(معاويه بن نوفل) told his men; Let's attack!

56
00:04:11,617 --> 00:04:17,218
And the rest of the tribe of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) refused.

57
00:04:17,775 --> 00:04:19,958
And some of their chiefs refused,

58
00:04:19,998 --> 00:04:26,272
it was only Muawiyyah Bin Nofal(معاويه بن نوفل) and his followers who did this, not all Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر).

59
00:04:26,518 --> 00:04:32,101
It is important to keep this in mind because of the implications of it.

60
00:04:32,513 --> 00:04:36,225
When can war be waged against an enemy.

61
00:04:36,690 --> 00:04:43,237
So, here it is clearly stated that not all of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) were involved in this betrayal.

62
00:04:43,702 --> 00:04:48,983
Because it is a betrayal there is a peace treaty with Muhammad ﷺ

63
00:04:49,445 --> 00:04:52,228
between Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Muhammadﷺ, Sulha Al- Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبية)

64
00:04:52,587 --> 00:04:55,040
and Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) and Khuza'a(خزاعه) are part of that treaty,

65
00:04:55,366 --> 00:04:59,411
because they are both in alliance with the two parties of the agreement.

66
00:04:59,726 --> 00:05:03,502
So, what Muawiyyah(معاويه) is doing is a breach of this agreement.

67
00:05:03,565 --> 00:05:06,375
It's a breach of the truce of Al-Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبية).

68
00:05:06,603 --> 00:05:10,101
Therefore many of his tribe refused to join in.

69
00:05:10,261 --> 00:05:15,451
And as I also mentioned, the other chiefs of the tribe also did not participate in this.

70
00:05:16,293 --> 00:05:18,537
So, they killed some of the people of Khuza'a(خزاعه).

71
00:05:18,577 --> 00:05:20,649
Khuza'a(خزاعه) fled and entered into Al-Haram(ألحرم).

72
00:05:21,034 --> 00:05:24,429
So now, they are within the sacred bounds.

73
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:28,436
And the Haram(حرم) is recognized by the people of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة),

74
00:05:28,799 --> 00:05:37,153
they used to consider to be a grave sin, to kill anybody inside Al-Haram(ألحرم) or to kill anybody during the holy months.

75
00:05:37,511 --> 00:05:40,865
There were four months of the year, when no killing should happen.

76
00:05:41,048 --> 00:05:47,028
And there is the boundary surrounding Makkah, where no one should be killed and that is all throughout the year.

77
00:05:47,188 --> 00:05:51,031
While within the four months all over Arabia no killing should happen.

78
00:05:51,637 --> 00:05:55,379
So, now the people of Khuza'a(خزاعه) are already within Al-Haram(ألحرم).

79
00:05:55,665 --> 00:06:02,773
So the people of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر), who are killing the people of Khuza'a(خزاعه) with Muawiyah(معاويه),

80
00:06:03,021 --> 00:06:04,055
They told ’Muawiyah(معاويه);

81
00:06:04,095 --> 00:06:07,391
يَا مُعَاوِيَّه اِلَهَكْ اِلَهَكْ ، اَلْحَرَمْ اَلْحَرَمْ

82
00:06:08,004 --> 00:06:10,749
They are warning Muawiyah(معاويه)

83
00:06:10,789 --> 00:06:14,010
and they are in fact amazed at what Muawiyah(معاويه) is doing, they said;

84
00:06:14,249 --> 00:06:17,555
اِنَّ قَدْ دَخَلْنَا الْحَرَمْ، اِلَهَكَ اِلَهَكَ يَا نُوْفَلْ

85
00:06:18,301 --> 00:06:24,044
So, they told him we have entered into Al-Haram(ألحرم) your God, your God, Muawiyah(معاويه).

86
00:06:24,189 --> 00:06:25,317
They're reminding him.

87
00:06:26,079 --> 00:06:27,326
What did Muawiyah(معاويه) say?

88
00:06:27,366 --> 00:06:29,277
And look at the answer that he gave them.

89
00:06:29,386 --> 00:06:37,253
لَا اِلَهَ الْيَوْمْ بَنِيْ بَكْرْ، أَصِيْبُوْا ثَأرَكُمْ فَلِعَمْرِيْ اِنَّكُمْ لَتَسْرِفُوْنَ فِي الّحَرَمْ أَفَلَا تُصِيْبُوْنَ فِيْهِ ثَأرَكُمْ

90
00:06:37,585 --> 00:06:42,934
He said: There is no God today, O Banni Bakr(بني بكر), Seek your revenge.

91
00:06:43,268 --> 00:06:46,514
 In the name of Allah, you are stealing from people inside Al-Haram(ألحرم).

92
00:06:46,698 --> 00:06:49,794
Wouldn't you seek your revenge, there in.

93
00:06:50,087 --> 00:06:53,326
Muawiya(معاويه) is justifying what he's doing and telling them;

94
00:06:53,650 --> 00:06:56,275
You already steal inside Al-Haram(ألحرم),

95
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:59,521
how come now, you're complaining that we're inside Al-Haram(ألحرم).

96
00:06:59,791 --> 00:07:03,197
Now, we have a point of killing and that is we are seeking our revenge.

97
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:09,620
And the people of Khuza'a(خزاعه) fled from Muawiyah(معاويه) and his men

98
00:07:09,953 --> 00:07:12,071
until, they entered into Makkah itself

99
00:07:12,310 --> 00:07:17,691
and they sought refuge in the house of the Badeel Bin Warqah Al-Khuza'e(بديل بن ورقع ألخزاعي).

100
00:07:17,890 --> 00:07:21,333
This is a man from Khuza'a(خزاعه) who used to live inside Makkah.

101
00:07:21,595 --> 00:07:27,513
So they went to him and sought refuge in him from this crime that was committed against them.

102
00:07:28,642 --> 00:07:34,812
Amr Bin Salim Al-Khuza'e(عمرو بن سالم ألخزاعي) one of the men of Khuza'a(خزاعه), he immediately went to Madina,

103
00:07:35,611 --> 00:07:40,261
to convey the news of what's happened to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

104
00:07:41,196 --> 00:07:46,214
And he delivered the news to Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه, in lines of poetry,

105
00:07:47,203 --> 00:07:51,370
reminding Muhammadﷺ with their alliance

106
00:07:51,874 --> 00:07:58,424
and reminding him with the alliance that they had with his great grandfather, Hashim(هاشم).

107
00:07:59,019 --> 00:08:01,210
What was the response of Rasool Allah ﷺ.?

108
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:07,428
If such a situation was brought to the leaders of today,

109
00:08:07,908 --> 00:08:11,265
they would probably say let's take it to the United Nations,

110
00:08:12,056 --> 00:08:14,850
Or let's see what the Security Council will say,

111
00:08:15,377 --> 00:08:18,064
Or let's consult with international community,

112
00:08:18,365 --> 00:08:24,028
or other ways of getting out of their responsibility.

113
00:08:24,774 --> 00:08:27,964
When Amr Bin Salim(عمرو بن سالم) presented this to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

114
00:08:27,988 --> 00:08:31,776
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him a clear and direct and decisive answer.

115
00:08:31,816 --> 00:08:32,578
He told him;

116
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:34,855
نُصِرْتَ يَا عَمْرُوْ بِنْ سَالِمْ

117
00:08:35,117 --> 00:08:35,817
One word,

118
00:08:36,087 --> 00:08:41,429
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; You've been helped, Amr Bin Salim(عمرو بن سالم). That's it!

119
00:08:42,159 --> 00:08:42,990
You will get the help!

120
00:08:43,179 --> 00:08:44,373
He didn't tell him. How?

121
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:47,426
He didn't give him the details, he gave him this promise.

122
00:08:47,876 --> 00:08:49,325
نُصِرْتَ يَا عَمْرُوْ بِنْ سَالِمْ

123
00:08:49,931 --> 00:08:52,865
You are helped, it's done, it's over.

124
00:08:53,604 --> 00:08:57,186
And then a cloud passed by and Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

125
00:08:57,479 --> 00:09:03,039
This cloud is giving me the glad tidings of support and help to Banni Ka'ab(بني كعب).

126
00:09:03,207 --> 00:09:05,451
Banni Ka'ab(بني كعب), are the people of Khuza'a(خزاعه).

127
00:09:06,072 --> 00:09:12,390
Back to something that I mentioned, see the statement of Ibn Is'haq(إبن إسحاق), he said:

128
00:09:12,430 --> 00:09:21,424
فَخَرَجَ نَوْفَلُ بْنُ مُعَاوِيَةَ الدِّيلِيُّ فِي قَوْمِه ، وَهُوَ يَوْمَئِذٍ سَيِّدُهُمْ وَقَائِدُهُمْ، وَلَيْسَ كُلُّ بَنِي بَكْرٍ تَابَعَهُ

129
00:09:22,022 --> 00:09:23,134
Ibn Ishaaq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says;

130
00:09:23,372 --> 00:09:29,443
Muawiya Bin Nofal Ad-Dayhli(معاويه بن نوفل الدؤلي), went out with his people and he was their leader,

131
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:33,389
but not all of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) followed him.

132
00:09:34,573 --> 00:09:38,108
Even though, not all of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) followed Muawiyah(معاويه).

133
00:09:38,479 --> 00:09:46,660
Rasool Allah ﷺ considered, what happened to be sufficient enough for the covenant to be ended

134
00:09:47,102 --> 00:09:52,241
and for war to be announced against the people of Makkah.

135
00:09:52,542 --> 00:09:57,550
And he also did not announced to the people of Makkah, his intentions of attacking them.

136
00:09:57,590 --> 00:09:59,955
In fact, it was done secretly.

137
00:10:00,305 --> 00:10:05,337
It was clandestine operation, Rasool Allah ﷺ made Dua(دُعَا) to Allah;

138
00:10:05,615 --> 00:10:13,679
O Allah concealed the news and blind their eyes from seeing us or knowing about our advance.

139
00:10:14,174 --> 00:10:19,170
And that is what happened the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) only knew about the advance of the Muslim army

140
00:10:19,210 --> 00:10:21,152
 when they were in the outskirts of Makkah.

141
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:28,105
Therefore, not all of the population need to be supportive of what the government does

142
00:10:28,492 --> 00:10:33,160
for it to be considered a breach of covenant between them and the Muslims.

143
00:10:33,632 --> 00:10:38,329
For example, if people come out in demonstration against war

144
00:10:38,708 --> 00:10:41,294
or some of the government is against war,

145
00:10:41,892 --> 00:10:48,343
as long as part of the government has taken the official stance of attacking the Muslims,

146
00:10:48,472 --> 00:10:56,839
the leader of the Muslims has the right to announce war and fight against this particular nation.

147
00:10:57,578 --> 00:11:02,507
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ immediately, after that he started preparation.

148
00:11:03,097 --> 00:11:07,953
Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه, he visited his daughter Ayesha(عائشه)

149
00:11:08,403 --> 00:11:14,839
and he saw her sifting and preparing wheat for the travel of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

150
00:11:15,450 --> 00:11:19,495
It might have been particular food that Rasool Allah ﷺ would carry with him

151
00:11:19,874 --> 00:11:21,170
when he's traveling in a Ghazwa(غزوة).

152
00:11:21,588 --> 00:11:26,778
So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) when he saw her doing that he knew that Rasool Allah ﷺ is intending on fighting someone

153
00:11:26,818 --> 00:11:27,898
 but he didn't know whom?

154
00:11:28,261 --> 00:11:31,202
In one narration, it says that he asked Ayesha(عائشه) and told her;

155
00:11:31,714 --> 00:11:35,204
Is Rasool Allah ﷺ planning on a conquest.

156
00:11:35,521 --> 00:11:36,897
So, Ayesha(عائشه) said: Yes.

157
00:11:37,186 --> 00:11:39,495
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) asked her: Is it the Romans?

158
00:11:39,685 --> 00:11:40,885
She didn't answer.

159
00:11:41,083 --> 00:11:43,440
Then he asked her: Is it such and such?

160
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,447
She didn't answer.

161
00:11:44,816 --> 00:11:47,383
So, she was keeping it secret.

162
00:11:47,598 --> 00:11:50,109
In another narration he asked her and she didn't know.

163
00:11:50,816 --> 00:11:55,074
And then Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) waited until, Rasool Allah ﷺ came and he asked him.

164
00:11:55,114 --> 00:12:01,422
And Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, Obviously Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is the most prominent advisor of Rasool Allah ﷺ

165
00:12:01,687 --> 00:12:04,873
and he confides, his secrets to him.

166
00:12:05,213 --> 00:12:10,908
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), that I'm going to attack Makkah, attack Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

167
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:12,920
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

168
00:12:13,162 --> 00:12:14,599
 كَأنِّيْ بِأَبِيْ سُفَيَّانْ

169
00:12:14,892 --> 00:12:22,592
As if I can see Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) coming to you, to ask for a renewal of our pact.

170
00:12:22,846 --> 00:12:26,103
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحان الله), that is exactly what happened

171
00:12:26,732 --> 00:12:32,023
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) after what's happened, he started his travel towards Madina.

172
00:12:32,613 --> 00:12:35,595
When Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر) were killing Khuza'a(خزاعه).

173
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:43,608
It says that they provided under the cover of darkness, support to the people of Bannu Bakr(بنوبكر)

174
00:12:44,096 --> 00:12:45,998
and they provided them with arms,

175
00:12:46,329 --> 00:12:49,290
and in fact, it says that some of them participated in the killing.

176
00:12:49,693 --> 00:12:53,367
And they said: It is night and no one will see what happened.

177
00:12:53,622 --> 00:12:57,885
And therefore Muhammadﷺ will not know about our participation.

178
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:02,598
They're ignorant to the fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ is the Messenger of Allah,

179
00:13:02,735 --> 00:13:05,412
and that he's receiving Wahii(وحي) from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

180
00:13:05,452 --> 00:13:09,013
The news was delivered to Muhammadﷺ

181
00:13:09,362 --> 00:13:16,717
and Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) now became extremely worried that Rasool Allah ﷺ might attack.

182
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:20,543
So, he immediately traveled to Madina to beg,

183
00:13:20,788 --> 00:13:28,630
 literally beg, Rasool Allah ﷺ to renew the pact and to increase in its time limit.

184
00:13:28,918 --> 00:13:30,793
The time frame that we're talking about now,

185
00:13:31,155 --> 00:13:37,602
we are 17 or 18 months after the signing of Sulh Al-Hudaybiyah(صلح الحديبية)

186
00:13:37,965 --> 00:13:40,652
So, Sulh Al-Hudaybiyah(صلح الحديبية) was for 10 years.

187
00:13:41,102 --> 00:13:48,394
And now, within little over a year, they have already committed a breach to the agreement.

188
00:13:49,179 --> 00:13:52,222
So, this is what the kuffar(كفار) have done.

189
00:13:52,412 --> 00:13:58,038
And now, they want to apologize for what happened, as if an apology would do.

190
00:13:58,228 --> 00:14:02,389
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), on the way he met with Badeel Bin Warkaa(بديل بن ورقه).

191
00:14:02,429 --> 00:14:03,060
Who's Badeel(بديل)?

192
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:09,007
Remember we said he's the man in Makkah, whom the people of Khuza'a(خزاعه) sought refuge in his house.

193
00:14:09,692 --> 00:14:11,735
So, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) told him; Where did you come from?

194
00:14:11,775 --> 00:14:16,130
He said: I just visited some people of Khuza'a(خزاعه) on the coast.

195
00:14:16,728 --> 00:14:21,885
Badeel Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقه), actually, just came back from Madina.

196
00:14:22,085 --> 00:14:25,889
He also went there to tell Rasool Allah ﷺ about what happened.

197
00:14:26,339 --> 00:14:33,793
So, the Kuffar(كفار) and the Muslims of Khuza'a(خزاعه), they were going to Rasool Allah ﷺ, seeking his assistance and help.

198
00:14:34,073 --> 00:14:39,611
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), he wasn't sure of, what Badeel(بديل) was telling him

199
00:14:40,178 --> 00:14:43,136
and he had suspicions about it.

200
00:14:43,445 --> 00:14:45,294
So, he waited until, Badeel(بديل) left

201
00:14:45,535 --> 00:14:49,455
and then he went to the place where Badeel(بديل)'s camel was

202
00:14:49,849 --> 00:14:54,327
and he took some of the droppings of the camel and he crushed it, in his hands.

203
00:14:54,732 --> 00:14:58,849
And he found, in it crushed date seeds.

204
00:14:59,104 --> 00:15:01,874
And this is something that is fed to the camels in Madina.

205
00:15:02,070 --> 00:15:05,679
Because Madina is where the date palms are grown.

206
00:15:05,941 --> 00:15:10,930
They don't grow in other parts of Hijaaz(ألحجاز) such as Makkah or in the land of Khuza'a(خزاعه)

207
00:15:10,970 --> 00:15:15,809
 because, Badeel Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقه), he said: I just came back from visiting people of Khuza'a(خزاعه).

208
00:15:15,922 --> 00:15:21,737
So, when Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), saw the crushed pieces of date seeds in the droppings of the camel.

209
00:15:22,108 --> 00:15:25,491
He said: Badeel(بديل), he just come back from Madina.

210
00:15:26,479 --> 00:15:28,202
So, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) went to Madina,

211
00:15:28,659 --> 00:15:29,600
where would he go?

212
00:15:29,663 --> 00:15:32,917
He would obviously go to the house of his daughter, Umm Habiba(اُمّ حبيبه),

213
00:15:33,205 --> 00:15:36,649
who was the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Umm-Al-Mo'mineen(أم المؤمنين).

214
00:15:36,982 --> 00:15:39,790
When he entered into the house, there was a rug on the floor.

215
00:15:39,830 --> 00:15:41,981
He wanted to sit on that rug.

216
00:15:42,303 --> 00:15:47,722
Umm Habiba(اُمّ حبيبه) pulled it away from him and wrapped it, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said;

217
00:15:48,403 --> 00:15:53,852
مَا أَدْرِيْ أَرَغَبْتِ بِيْ عَنْ هَذَا الْفِرَاشْ أَمْ أرْغِبْتَ بِهِ عَنِّيْ ؟

218
00:15:54,425 --> 00:16:00,609
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) told his daughter; I don't know, did you wrapped and take away this rug,

219
00:16:01,050 --> 00:16:09,074
because you see it not be fitting for me or you see me not be fitting for the rug.?

220
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:10,452
Umm Habiba(اُمّ حبيبه) said;

221
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:15,309
 بَلْ هُوَ فِرَاشِ رَسُول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وَأَنْتَ مُشْرِكٌ نَجِسْ

222
00:16:15,591 --> 00:16:17,751
فَلَمْ أُحِبَّ أَنْ تَجْلِسْ عَلَى فِرَاشِه

223
00:16:18,115 --> 00:16:21,964
Umm Habiba(اُمّ حبيبه) said: This rug belongs to Rasool Allah ﷺ

224
00:16:22,288 --> 00:16:26,385
and you are a dirty Polytheist, you are a dirty Mushrik(مشرك),

225
00:16:26,787 --> 00:16:31,181
and I don't want you to sit on the rug of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

226
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:34,987
This is the loyalty that they had towards Rasool Allah ﷺ

227
00:16:35,011 --> 00:16:38,147
Umm Habiba(اُمّ حبيبه) is speaking to her father, her own father.

228
00:16:38,557 --> 00:16:42,201
But she did not even want him and he is her father

229
00:16:42,487 --> 00:16:45,779
to sit on the rug that belongs to Rasool Allah ﷺ. Why?

230
00:16:46,135 --> 00:16:50,325
Because she understands that Kuffr(كفر) is Najasa(نجاسه).

231
00:16:50,548 --> 00:16:52,887
This is the Walaa(ولآء) and Bara(برآة) that the Muslim should have.

232
00:16:53,657 --> 00:16:57,332
And Umm Habiba(اُمّ حبيبه) is not dealing with a commoner from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

233
00:16:57,372 --> 00:17:02,899
she's dealing with the leader the chief of the tribe, of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

234
00:17:03,473 --> 00:17:06,001
And these were her words to him.

235
00:17:06,385 --> 00:17:08,101
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) was shocked and he said;

236
00:17:08,125 --> 00:17:10,972
يَا بُنَيَّ وَلله لَقَدْ أَصَابَكِ بَعْدِيْ شَر

237
00:17:11,476 --> 00:17:16,768
O my daughter, in the name of Allah, evil has befell you.

238
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:22,704
And then Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he told him;

239
00:17:23,075 --> 00:17:26,689
I want to add to the time

240
00:17:27,279 --> 00:17:32,993
or I want to renew the pact and increase the time of our truce.

241
00:17:33,208 --> 00:17:36,776
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; Did something happened from your end?

242
00:17:37,022 --> 00:17:41,121
I mean, we already have an agreement and it's for 10 years, what's the point of coming now.?

243
00:17:41,532 --> 00:17:45,172
After 17 or 18 months asking for it to be renewed?

244
00:17:45,778 --> 00:17:49,301
The agreement is already there, so what's the point of coming here?

245
00:17:49,868 --> 00:17:53,508
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان); Did anything happened?

246
00:17:53,974 --> 00:17:56,043
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said: No, Everything is fine.

247
00:17:56,264 --> 00:17:57,733
Rasool Allah ﷺ walked away.

248
00:17:57,939 --> 00:17:59,180
Rasool Ullah ignored him,

249
00:17:59,490 --> 00:18:03,143
Rasool Ullah walked away from Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and didn't respond back to him.

250
00:18:04,133 --> 00:18:09,571
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) then went to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), and he told him; I want you to speak to Rasool Allah ﷺ

251
00:18:09,724 --> 00:18:15,577
to intercede on my behalf and to speak to Rasool Allah ﷺ and ask him to renew the pact.

252
00:18:16,011 --> 00:18:16,857
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) told him;

253
00:18:16,897 --> 00:18:17,718
 مَا أَنَا بِفَاعِلْ

254
00:18:17,868 --> 00:18:19,026
I would not do that.

255
00:18:19,402 --> 00:18:21,565
And then Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) went to Umar(عُمر).

256
00:18:22,173 --> 00:18:24,628
Now, they all know who Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) is,

257
00:18:24,950 --> 00:18:28,219
they know the nature and the character of Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب).

258
00:18:28,244 --> 00:18:34,179
But I want you to think about the state of humiliation and humbleness.

259
00:18:34,605 --> 00:18:36,517
And when I say humbleness

260
00:18:36,557 --> 00:18:41,119
because the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) they used to deal with the Muslims, with such pride and arrogance.

261
00:18:41,412 --> 00:18:46,337
We shouldn't even use the word humbleness, it is humiliation.

262
00:18:46,377 --> 00:18:51,538
 He came into humiliated state begging the Muslims to renew the pact.

263
00:18:51,578 --> 00:18:53,699
I want you to think about this for a moment

264
00:18:53,968 --> 00:18:59,662
and compare to the situation of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) when the Muslims were in Makkah

265
00:18:59,932 --> 00:19:06,086
 and see how low they have became, a few years later.

266
00:19:06,559 --> 00:19:08,964
Now, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) himself, who was a leader,

267
00:19:09,004 --> 00:19:14,436
who used to see himself higher than the level of speaking to the Muslims.

268
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:19,267
Now, he's going from house to house begging them to go to Rasool Allah ﷺ

269
00:19:19,307 --> 00:19:21,643
because Rasool Ullah ignored him, Rasool Ullah just walked away.

270
00:19:22,257 --> 00:19:24,387
So, now Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) goes to Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب)

271
00:19:25,024 --> 00:19:30,664
and he tells him, I want you to intercede on our behalf and to ask Rasool Allah ﷺ to renew the pact.

272
00:19:30,704 --> 00:19:31,862
 Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب), he said;

273
00:19:31,886 --> 00:19:33,228
أَنَا أَشْفَعُ لَكُمْ

274
00:19:33,786 --> 00:19:36,033
You want me to intercede on your behalf.

275
00:19:36,287 --> 00:19:42,039
أَنَا أَشْفَعُ لَكُمْ عِنْدَ رَسُول الله فَوَالله لَوْ لَمْ اَجِدْ لَكُمْ إِلَّا الذَّرْ لَجَاهِدْتُكُمْ بِه

276
00:19:42,575 --> 00:19:46,835
You want me to intercede on your behalf with Rasool Allah ﷺ

277
00:19:46,875 --> 00:19:51,214
In the name of Allah, if I find nothing but ants to fight your with, I would fight you.

278
00:19:52,036 --> 00:19:56,637
If I have no men to fight you and I have to fight you with ants, then I would do so.

279
00:19:57,266 --> 00:19:58,373
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) left.

280
00:19:58,706 --> 00:20:03,302
And then Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) he went to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

281
00:20:03,817 --> 00:20:04,976
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told him;

282
00:20:05,016 --> 00:20:06,792
 وَيْحَكَ يَا أَبَا سُفِيَّانْ

283
00:20:07,054 --> 00:20:13,403
وَاللهِ لَقَدْ عَزَمَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عَلى أَمْرٍ مَا نَسْتَطِيْعُ أَنْ نُكَلِّمُه’ فِيْهْ

284
00:20:14,197 --> 00:20:16,509
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان);

285
00:20:16,731 --> 00:20:19,622
Woe to you Abu Sufian(ابوسفيان) in the name of Allah,

286
00:20:19,892 --> 00:20:25,957
Rasool Allah ﷺ has made his decision to do something and we cannot talk to him about it.

287
00:20:26,446 --> 00:20:29,669
In other words when Rasool Allah ﷺ decides in a particular matter,

288
00:20:30,139 --> 00:20:34,567
we cannot go to Rasool Allah ﷺ and ask him to change his mind, it's over with.

289
00:20:35,212 --> 00:20:39,638
Shura(شورى) is before the decision is made, after the decision is made, it is done.

290
00:20:40,033 --> 00:20:41,851
فَاِذَا عَزَمْتَ فَتَوَكَّل اِلَى الله

291
00:20:42,183 --> 00:20:45,018
When you decide and have Tawaqqul(توكل) on Allah and go ahead.

292
00:20:45,811 --> 00:20:49,606
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), he visited Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) in his house and this was before Hijab(حجاب).

293
00:20:50,118 --> 00:20:53,527
So, Fatima(فاطمه) was there and she was playing with her son Al-Hassan(الحسن).

294
00:20:54,007 --> 00:20:57,639
Al-Hassan(الحسن) was a child at that time and she was playing with him.

295
00:20:58,186 --> 00:21:03,088
When Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) spoke to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told him that it's done.

296
00:21:03,553 --> 00:21:06,540
Look at what Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) did, he spoke to Fatima(فاطمه) and he said;

297
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:15,544
يَا بنت محمد هَلْ لَكِي انْ تَأْمُرِيْ بُنَيَّكِي هَذَا فَيُجِيْرُ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ فَيَكُوْنَ سَيِّد الْعَرَبِ إِلَى آخِرِ الدَّهَرْ؟

298
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:17,597
O Daughter of Muhammad(محمد),

299
00:21:18,224 --> 00:21:25,102
Would you ask this son of yours to give protection between people

300
00:21:25,328 --> 00:21:29,838
and that would make him the leader of the Arabs, until the end of time.

301
00:21:30,314 --> 00:21:39,197
I mean, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) is talking to Fatima(فاطمه) to ask this child Al-Hassan(الحسن), who's playing to give protection.

302
00:21:39,850 --> 00:21:46,538
قَالَتْ وَالله مَا بَلَغَ بُنَيَّ ذَلِكْ أَنْ يُّجِيْرَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ وَمَا يَجِيْرَ اَحَدً عَلَى النَّبِى صلى الله عليه وسلم

303
00:21:47,198 --> 00:21:51,960
She said: In the name of Allah, My son is too young to do that.

304
00:21:52,527 --> 00:21:56,923
And then she told him and nobody can give protection in the presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

305
00:21:57,295 --> 00:22:03,141
I mean, if Rasool Ullah decides to fight, we cannot give protection contrary to his decision.

306
00:22:03,848 --> 00:22:08,139
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) is in a state of desperation, you can see from his actions.

307
00:22:08,186 --> 00:22:11,758
I mean, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) is a wise strong leader.

308
00:22:12,127 --> 00:22:15,651
But he is now acting in a way that is confused

309
00:22:16,144 --> 00:22:19,112
for Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) to ask such a foolish request

310
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:24,618
shows you the state of despair that Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and the people of Quraish(قريش) reached.

311
00:22:25,755 --> 00:22:26,167
He said;

312
00:22:26,207 --> 00:22:30,318
 يَا أَبَا الْحَسَنْ إِنِّيْ أَرَى الْأَمُوْرْ قَدْ اَشْتَدَّتْ عَلَيَّ فَانْصَحْنِيْ

313
00:22:30,508 --> 00:22:33,915
O Abul Hassan(ابوالحسن), I see that things are becoming tough.

314
00:22:34,365 --> 00:22:37,558
Things are becoming tight. Give me your advice.

315
00:22:38,015 --> 00:22:41,510
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) doesn't have anything to advise him, but he told him.

316
00:22:41,534 --> 00:22:43,178
وَالله مَا أَعْلَمْ شَيْئًا يُغْنِيْ عَنْكَ

317
00:22:43,706 --> 00:22:46,431
In the name of Allah, I know nothing that would do you any good.

318
00:22:46,834 --> 00:22:52,604
وَلَكِنَّكِ سَيِّدُ بَنِيْ كِنَانَةْ فَقُمْ فَأَجِرْ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ ثُمَّ الْحَقْ بِأَرْضِكْ

319
00:22:52,843 --> 00:22:56,525
He said; But you are the leader of the children of Kinanah(كنانه).

320
00:22:56,958 --> 00:23:02,364
So, go to the Masjid(مسجد) and give protection, among the people and then go back to your land.

321
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:05,909
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) respond back, he said;

322
00:23:06,366 --> 00:23:08,310
أَوْتَرَى ذَلِكَ مُغْنِيْ عَنِّيْ شَيْئًا ؟

323
00:23:08,334 --> 00:23:09,996
Do you think that that would do me any good?

324
00:23:10,438 --> 00:23:11,780
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told him; No.

325
00:23:12,073 --> 00:23:12,921
وَاللهِ مَا أَظُنْ

326
00:23:12,961 --> 00:23:14,381
I don't think that it would do any good.

327
00:23:14,827 --> 00:23:16,417
وَلَكِنْ لَّا أَجِدُ لَكَ غَيْرَ ذَلِكْ

328
00:23:16,441 --> 00:23:18,171
But I find nothing else to tell you.

329
00:23:18,722 --> 00:23:22,092
As if Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is telling him, I have no advice to give you.

330
00:23:22,377 --> 00:23:26,299
And this advice that I gave you wouldn't really do you any good.

331
00:23:26,672 --> 00:23:28,101
He is trying to get rid of him.

332
00:23:28,999 --> 00:23:34,646
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), even though Ali(علي) told him رضي الله عنه that this advice would do you no good

333
00:23:34,916 --> 00:23:37,507
he still followed the advice of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

334
00:23:37,547 --> 00:23:39,380
and he went to the Masjid(مسجد) and he stood in there.

335
00:23:39,709 --> 00:23:40,074
And he said,

336
00:23:40,114 --> 00:23:41,919
إِنِّيْ قَدْ أَجَرْتُ بَيْنَ النَّاسْ

337
00:23:42,142 --> 00:23:46,474
Now just a little bit of background on this issue of Ijarah(إجارة), offering protection.

338
00:23:46,826 --> 00:23:50,996
In the time of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) men who were leaders among their people

339
00:23:51,351 --> 00:23:56,001
would give their word in front of the people and say that I protect, so and so.

340
00:23:56,239 --> 00:23:59,379
Because of the honor of this person and because of his position.

341
00:23:59,711 --> 00:24:05,122
And because of his strength or the strength of his tribe, the people would accept that protection

342
00:24:05,344 --> 00:24:07,929
 and they would not go against it, they would honor his word.

343
00:24:08,410 --> 00:24:16,725
So, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) went to the Masjid(مسجد) and he did that in the Masjid(مسجد) of Al-Madina in Al-Masjid-e-Nabwi(مسجد النبوي)

344
00:24:17,264 --> 00:24:20,711
 but who is Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) in Madina Who cares about Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان).

345
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:25,285
Yes, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) is the leader of Kinaana(كنانه) but that doesn't mean anything in Madina.

346
00:24:25,678 --> 00:24:28,533
In Madina, the leader is Muhammadﷺ.

347
00:24:29,208 --> 00:24:31,602
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) doesn't carry any weight.

348
00:24:32,014 --> 00:24:35,889
So people were just passing by ignoring Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) completely.

349
00:24:36,703 --> 00:24:42,143
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) left, went back to Makkah and he met with the people of Makkah and told them;

350
00:24:42,538 --> 00:24:44,869
جِئْتُ محمدا فَكَلَّمْتَه’

351
00:24:45,170 --> 00:24:47,010
I came to Muhammad(محمد) and I spoke to him;

352
00:24:47,459 --> 00:24:48,809
فَلَمْ يَرُدْعَلَيْ شیئا

353
00:24:48,997 --> 00:24:50,449
He didn't give me any answer.

354
00:24:50,744 --> 00:24:55,736
ثُمًّ جِئْتُ اِبْنْ اَبِيْ قُحَافَةْ، فَوَالله مَا وجَدْتَه’ عِنْدَه’ خَيْرَا

355
00:24:55,951 --> 00:25:00,523
Then I went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and I didn't find any good with him.

356
00:25:01,059 --> 00:25:03,428
ثُمَّ جِئْتَ عُمَر فَوَجَدْتَّه’ أَعْدَى الْعَدُّوْ

357
00:25:03,529 --> 00:25:05,862
And then I went to Umar(عمر) and I found him the worst enemy.

358
00:25:06,382 --> 00:25:08,649
ثُمَّ جِئْتُ عَلِيّا فَوَجَدْتُّه’ أَلِيًّنْ الّقَوْمْ

359
00:25:08,739 --> 00:25:13,569
And then I went to Ali(علي), and I found him the softest among the people, I met.

360
00:25:13,989 --> 00:25:16,517
وَقَدْ أَشَارَ عَلَيَّ بِاَمْرٍ وَصَنَعْتُه’

361
00:25:17,013 --> 00:25:19,173
And he gave me advice to do something and I did it.

362
00:25:19,212 --> 00:25:22,350
فَوَالله مَا أَدْرِيْ هَلْ يُغْنِيْ عنِّيْ ذَالِكَ شَيْئًا أَمْ لَا ؟

363
00:25:22,886 --> 00:25:27,801
And then I followed his advice and I don't know whether it's going to do me any good or not.

364
00:25:28,488 --> 00:25:30,030
They told him, what did he tell you to do?

365
00:25:30,261 --> 00:25:32,639
قَالَ أَمَرَنِيْ أَنْ أُجِيْرَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ فَفَعَلْتِ

366
00:25:32,663 --> 00:25:35,016
He told me to offer protection and I did.

367
00:25:35,927 --> 00:25:37,230
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) told him;

368
00:25:37,254 --> 00:25:38,979
فَهَلْ أَجاَزَ ذَلِكَ مُحَمَّدْ ؟

369
00:25:39,003 --> 00:25:40,872
Did Muhammadﷺ approve that.?

370
00:25:41,078 --> 00:25:41,810
He said: No.

371
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:44,859
قَالُوْا وَيْحَكَ وَالله مَا زَادَكَ رَجُل أَنْ لَّعِبَ بِكْ

372
00:25:44,883 --> 00:25:47,987
Woe to you, Ali(علي) did nothing but make a fool out of you.

373
00:25:48,359 --> 00:25:51,136
He turned you into a toy, he played with you,

374
00:25:51,319 --> 00:25:55,662
he gave you an advice that would do you no good, in fact, it added to your humiliation.

375
00:25:56,479 --> 00:25:59,416
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) probably knew that but he had nothing else to do.

376
00:26:00,420 --> 00:26:04,671
As-Suhaili(أسهيلي) he comments here on the issue of offering protection because

377
00:26:05,058 --> 00:26:09,381
Fatima(فاطمه) said: That nobody can offer protection in the presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

378
00:26:09,933 --> 00:26:11,612
When Rasool Ullah has made the decision.

379
00:26:12,054 --> 00:26:13,888
While there's another Hadith(حديث) that says;

380
00:26:13,912 --> 00:26:16,581
وَيُجِيْرُ عَلَيْهِمْ اَدْنَاهُمْ

381
00:26:16,961 --> 00:26:20,737
Protection can be offered by the weakest of them.

382
00:26:21,210 --> 00:26:24,774
And we have the story of Umm Haanna(أم هانه),

383
00:26:24,997 --> 00:26:28,190
 when she gave protection and Rasool Allah ﷺ approved that protection.

384
00:26:28,499 --> 00:26:29,890
As-Suhaili(أسهيلي) says;

385
00:26:30,271 --> 00:26:32,986
 اَلْمُرَادْ بِالْحَدِيْثَ مَنْ يُجِيْرُ وَاحَدًا اَوْ نَفَرًا يَسِيْرًا

386
00:26:33,357 --> 00:26:37,120
As-Suhaili(أسهيلي) says that protection is approved and passed,

387
00:26:37,562 --> 00:26:41,050
when it's the protection of one individual or a small group.

388
00:26:41,075 --> 00:26:45,712
But here we're talking about offering protecction to an entire people.

389
00:26:45,950 --> 00:26:47,311
I mean, we're talking about Quraish(قريش).

390
00:26:47,710 --> 00:26:51,385
And that is why, no one can offer that protection.

391
00:26:51,945 --> 00:26:56,835
However, the protection can be offered for one person or a small number of people

392
00:26:56,860 --> 00:27:01,182
because, and we will talk about the situation of Umm Haanaa(ام هانه), she offer protection to two.

393
00:27:01,656 --> 00:27:02,879
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

394
00:27:03,170 --> 00:27:04,990
 اَجَرْنَا مَنْ اَجَرْتِ يَا اُمِّ هَانَى

395
00:27:05,023 --> 00:27:10,579
Rasool Allah ﷺ approved, and said we will protect whomever you offer, your protection to! Umm Haanna(أم هانه)!

396
00:27:11,010 --> 00:27:14,762
Again, we revisit the desperation of Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان).

397
00:27:15,313 --> 00:27:23,810
And since, we have now traveled through the years of Seerah-Nabwiyyah(سيرة النبويه) beginning from the initial days of Daw'ah(دعوة).

398
00:27:24,212 --> 00:27:29,656
And we talked about the oppression that the Muslims went through, in those difficult days in Makkah

399
00:27:29,919 --> 00:27:34,177
and the arrogance and pride of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

400
00:27:34,587 --> 00:27:41,753
And the way they used to belittle the Muslims and treat them as insignificant subjects.

401
00:27:42,196 --> 00:27:49,732
And now, you see Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), going from house to house begging for the Muslims to offer him protection.

402
00:27:50,103 --> 00:27:55,987
Dear brothers and sisters, if the Muslims today would get over the belief of

403
00:27:56,033 --> 00:27:57,951
"We Are weak and we can do nothing."

404
00:27:58,291 --> 00:28:02,309
The ones who are bombing the Muslims today would become like Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان)

405
00:28:02,670 --> 00:28:05,802
and come begging the Muslims for peace.

406
00:28:06,736 --> 00:28:10,539
But the Muslims need to get over the belief that they are weak

407
00:28:10,913 --> 00:28:14,789
and they are incapable of defending themselves.

408
00:28:15,170 --> 00:28:19,764
And this is not proper because Allahعزوجل says;

409
00:28:20,136 --> 00:28:29,682
وَلَا تَهِنُوا وَلَا تَحْزَنُوا وَأَنْتُمُ الْأَعْلَوْنَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ۝

410
00:28:30,148 --> 00:28:34,320
Allahعَزّوجَلّ in Surat Ul Al-Imran(سورة العمران) and this Ayah(آية) was revealed after the Ghazwa of Uhud(أحَد).

411
00:28:35,043 --> 00:28:38,491
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: And we talked about this Ayah(آية), when we talked about Ghazwa(غزوة) of Uhud(أحد).

412
00:28:39,152 --> 00:28:42,954
Don't see yourselves as in a humiliated state.

413
00:28:43,435 --> 00:28:46,551
And don't be sad when you are the highest.

414
00:28:46,583 --> 00:28:48,348
وَأَنْتُمُ الْأَعْلَوْنَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ۝

415
00:28:48,372 --> 00:28:51,462
If you are believers, you will be the highest, if you are believers

416
00:28:52,068 --> 00:28:56,968
but if you are disbelievers, or you don't follow the conditions of Eeman(إيمان),

417
00:28:57,128 --> 00:29:00,321
then yes, you could be in a state of humiliation.

418
00:29:00,345 --> 00:29:02,455
But a believer is always strong

419
00:29:02,479 --> 00:29:06,584
and remember that this Ayah(آية) was not revealed after a victory, it was revealed after a defeat.

420
00:29:07,339 --> 00:29:10,021
The defeat of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

421
00:29:10,916 --> 00:29:12,071
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

422
00:29:12,111 --> 00:29:13,014
 اصْبِرُوا وَصَابِرُوا

423
00:29:13,404 --> 00:29:27,331
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اِصْبِرُوا وَصَابِرُوا وَرَابِطُوا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ۝

424
00:29:27,732 --> 00:29:28,915
O you, who believe.

425
00:29:29,224 --> 00:29:32,419
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is ordering the believers who have Sabr(صبر), Isbiroo(إصبرو).

426
00:29:32,888 --> 00:29:37,634
Isbiroo(إصبرو) means Sabr(صبر), it's a command and order it's in the form of Fael Amr(فعل أمر),

427
00:29:38,235 --> 00:29:42,225
a verb of command Isbiroo(إصبرو), be patient.

428
00:29:42,964 --> 00:29:44,241
And then Wasabiro(وصابرو).

429
00:29:44,424 --> 00:29:48,608
Sabiroo(صابرو) is also derived from the root word of Sabr(صبر)

430
00:29:49,584 --> 00:29:52,283
but it's in the form of, what is called Mufaela(مفاعله).

431
00:29:53,452 --> 00:29:57,904
Mufaela(مفاعله) is when the verb is between two parties.

432
00:29:58,306 --> 00:30:03,361
So, for example, you have and all of these words that I'm going to give you are in the form of Mufaela(مفاعله).

433
00:30:03,676 --> 00:30:07,956
You have (مسارعه), wrestling in Arabic is called Musariah(مسارعه).

434
00:30:08,085 --> 00:30:10,333
Because it is between two parties.

435
00:30:10,931 --> 00:30:13,378
Mulaqamah(ملاقمه), boxing is called mulaqamah(ملاقمه),

436
00:30:13,402 --> 00:30:16,068
it is in the form of Mufaela(مفاعله) because it's between two parties.

437
00:30:16,640 --> 00:30:20,468
Muam'la(معامله), when you have a financial transaction

438
00:30:20,940 --> 00:30:24,471
because it is between two parties you call it Muam'la(معامله) or Mutajirah(متاجره).

439
00:30:24,898 --> 00:30:25,785
So on, and so forth.

440
00:30:25,825 --> 00:30:27,725
 So, here we have Wasabiroo(وصابرو).

441
00:30:28,064 --> 00:30:32,648
In other words, we need to outdo the enemy in patience.

442
00:30:32,672 --> 00:30:34,197
Because the enemy is patient.

443
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:37,674
Not only the Muslim is patient but also the enemy is patient.

444
00:30:37,862 --> 00:30:42,865
So even though Allahعزوجل order us to be patient, Isbiroo(إصبرو),

445
00:30:43,174 --> 00:30:45,879
but the next order is a repetition of patience.

446
00:30:45,919 --> 00:30:50,615
However here Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling us, it's not enough to be patient only

447
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:54,797
but you need to be more patient than the enemy you need to outdo the enemy in patience.

448
00:30:54,821 --> 00:30:58,381
Wasabiroo(وصابرو) and that is exactly what Rasool Allah ﷺ did.

449
00:30:58,736 --> 00:31:01,381
I mean, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), were patient and persistent

450
00:31:01,437 --> 00:31:06,514
because the word Sabrr(صبر) in Arabic not only means patience, but it also means persistence.

451
00:31:07,026 --> 00:31:11,529
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), for example, Abu Jahal(ابو جهل) was a very persistent individual.

452
00:31:11,553 --> 00:31:13,534
Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) was very persistent.

453
00:31:13,859 --> 00:31:20,017
Many of these leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who were fighting the Muslims were very persistent and committed to fighting Muslims.

454
00:31:20,144 --> 00:31:26,607
 They had this commitment and zeal and persistence and patience in fighting the religion of Allah.

455
00:31:27,083 --> 00:31:30,204
 But on the other hand Rasool Allah ﷺ was very patient

456
00:31:30,865 --> 00:31:35,590
and he was instructing and training the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم to be patient,

457
00:31:35,774 --> 00:31:38,449
when the companion came to Rasool Allah ﷺ

458
00:31:38,489 --> 00:31:40,376
and Rasool Allah ﷺ, was sitting next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

459
00:31:40,568 --> 00:31:42,383
and he told Rasool Allah ﷺ.

460
00:31:42,755 --> 00:31:45,136
اَلا تَدْعُوْلَنَا ، اَلَا تَسْتَنْصِرلَنَا

461
00:31:45,161 --> 00:31:49,474
O Rasool Ullah! Aren't you going to ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give us support?

462
00:31:49,598 --> 00:31:52,852
Aren't you going to ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give us victory?

463
00:31:52,892 --> 00:31:55,030
Because they have suffered a lot.

464
00:31:55,308 --> 00:31:58,840
So, the Sahabi(صحابي) is asking Rasool Allah ﷺ to make Dua(دُعَا) to Allah.

465
00:31:59,109 --> 00:32:03,321
That Allah elevates from us, takes away from us, this pain and suffering we're going through.

466
00:32:04,161 --> 00:32:06,703
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not say yes, I will make that Dua(دُعَا)!

467
00:32:06,728 --> 00:32:11,996
Rasool Allah ﷺ, sat up and he was angry and you could see anger in his face and he said;

468
00:32:12,641 --> 00:32:16,645
لَقَدْ كَانَ يُؤتی بِمَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكُمْ فَيُوضَعَ الْمِنْشَارَ عَلَى رَأْسِهِ

469
00:32:17,103 --> 00:32:19,656
They would bring a man from the nations before you

470
00:32:19,696 --> 00:32:25,758
and they would place the saw or the knife on top of his head and he would be split in half.

471
00:32:26,153 --> 00:32:27,695
فَلَا يَرُدُّه’ ذَالِكَ عَنْ دِيْنِكْ

472
00:32:28,066 --> 00:32:30,473
And that would not make him give up his religion.

473
00:32:30,930 --> 00:32:34,399
And they would bring a man from the nations before you and he would be combed.

474
00:32:34,423 --> 00:32:35,965
فيُمْشَطُ بِأَمْشَاطِ الْحَدِيدِ

475
00:32:35,990 --> 00:32:38,927
He would be combed with combs of steel.

476
00:32:39,322 --> 00:32:41,355
مَا بَيْنَ لَحْمِهِ وَعَظَمِهِ وَعَصَبِهْ

477
00:32:41,664 --> 00:32:45,738
That would comb away his nerves and his flesh from the bones.

478
00:32:46,094 --> 00:32:47,573
فَلَا يَرُدُّه’ ذَالِكَ عَنْ دِيْنِكْ

479
00:32:47,818 --> 00:32:50,026
And that would not make him give up his religion.

480
00:32:50,869 --> 00:32:52,453
وَلِيُتِمَّنَّ الله وَهَذَا الْاَمْرَ

481
00:32:52,744 --> 00:32:56,494
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ will give victory, to this religion of His.

482
00:32:56,959 --> 00:33:02,660
حَتَّى يَسِيرَ الرَّاكِبُ مِنْ صَنْعَاءَ إِلَى حَضْرَمَوْتَ لَا يَخَافُ إِلَّا اللَّهَ وَالذِّئْبَ عَلَى غَنَمِهِ،

483
00:33:02,968 --> 00:33:08,166
Until, the traveler would travel from San'a(صنعاء) to Hazara Al-Maot(حزرالموت) fearing no one but Allah

484
00:33:08,452 --> 00:33:11,287
and the wolves on his sheep.

485
00:33:11,799 --> 00:33:14,232
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is training the Sahabah(صحابه) to be patient.

486
00:33:14,449 --> 00:33:16,644
Eventually Allah will give you a victory.

487
00:33:16,668 --> 00:33:18,271
و الْعَاقِبَةَ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ

488
00:33:18,295 --> 00:33:21,774
The end would belong to the believers, but you have to be patient.

489
00:33:22,833 --> 00:33:25,227
And you have to give destiny, it's time.

490
00:33:25,490 --> 00:33:26,669
Don't be in a hurry.

491
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:31,206
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has destined things to happen in a certain way.

492
00:33:31,507 --> 00:33:34,151
We should not go against the Qadar(قدر) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

493
00:33:34,491 --> 00:33:37,488
Let everything take its time, eventually the Muslims would win.

494
00:33:37,679 --> 00:33:43,073
We shouldn't be in a hurry, we shouldn't hasten things to happen, they will happen with the Qadar(قدر) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

495
00:33:43,143 --> 00:33:44,881
أَتَىٰ أَمْرُ اللَّهِ فَلَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوهُ ۚ

496
00:33:45,158 --> 00:33:51,220
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: The command of Allah, whatever Allah has destined will come, don't hasten it.

497
00:33:51,974 --> 00:33:56,976
And the patience of the Muslims is now bearing it's fruits.

498
00:33:57,683 --> 00:34:04,016
Now, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) is coming alone into Madina, begging the Muslims to give him peace

499
00:34:04,273 --> 00:34:05,902
 and the Muslims are ignoring him.

500
00:34:06,609 --> 00:34:13,075
So, when the Muslims of today keep on feeding the Ummah(امة) that you are in a state of weakness

501
00:34:13,348 --> 00:34:16,318
that we are incapable, that the enemy is strong

502
00:34:16,564 --> 00:34:17,975
that we cannot do anything,

503
00:34:18,104 --> 00:34:21,096
that we are living in Makkah, we are like in the era of Makkah.

504
00:34:21,306 --> 00:34:26,214
And all of these concepts that instill in the Muslim mind fear

505
00:34:26,577 --> 00:34:32,103
and instill in the Muslim mind, a feeling of inferiority, and weakness and humiliation

506
00:34:32,499 --> 00:34:36,224
 that programs the Muslims to be weak and to accept oppression.

507
00:34:36,564 --> 00:34:40,311
How can we state that when we are one fifth the population of the world.

508
00:34:40,800 --> 00:34:43,689
When the Muslims are over 1 billion

509
00:34:44,490 --> 00:34:49,755
when the Muslims sit on the most valuable resources on the planet,

510
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:52,654
the oil of the world lives under the Muslims.

511
00:34:52,836 --> 00:34:58,371
It's like a living being that travels under the earth and goes and parks under the Muslim land.

512
00:34:59,039 --> 00:35:06,920
When the Muslims control some of the most important waterways and important parts of the world,

513
00:35:06,995 --> 00:35:10,746
when the Muslim lands spans all over the planet.

514
00:35:11,395 --> 00:35:16,055
How can the Muslim state that we are in a state of weakness, and in a state of humiliation?

515
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:19,392
Muslims need to break out of this way of thinking

516
00:35:19,583 --> 00:35:22,805
and realize the strength that they have,

517
00:35:22,997 --> 00:35:32,288
 and realize that they are not needy in terms of financial resources or numbers or land

518
00:35:32,574 --> 00:35:34,559
but what they need is Eeman(ايمان).

519
00:35:35,122 --> 00:35:37,338
What they need this trust in Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

520
00:35:37,629 --> 00:35:39,055
what they need is Tawaqqul(توكل).

521
00:35:39,559 --> 00:35:45,001
So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ is planning in secret to attack Makkah.

522
00:35:45,450 --> 00:35:50,657
That was initially but then he had to announce this to the Muslims to get prepared and ready

523
00:35:50,681 --> 00:35:56,220
but he told the Muslims, I mean, the Muslims knew that they're not supposed to speak about this

524
00:35:56,482 --> 00:35:58,180
that, they're supposed to keep this as a secret.

525
00:35:58,825 --> 00:36:06,127
One day Rasool Allah ﷺ, summoned Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام) and Al-Miqdad Bin Aswad(المقداد بن اسود),

526
00:36:06,604 --> 00:36:07,468
he told them;

527
00:36:07,597 --> 00:36:15,474
اِنْطَلِقُوا حَتَّى تَأْتُوا رَوْضَةَ خَاخٍ ، فَإِنَّ بِهَا ظَعِينَةً مَعَهَا كِتَابٌ فَخُذُوهُ مِنْهَا

528
00:36:16,510 --> 00:36:19,660
Go to a place called Roza At Khaakh(روضة الخاخ)

529
00:36:20,203 --> 00:36:26,167
you will find a woman and with her is a letter, bring that letter to me.

530
00:36:26,749 --> 00:36:32,463
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and the two men with him, Az-Zubair(الزبير) and Al-Miqdad(المقداد), they rushed.

531
00:36:32,711 --> 00:36:33,318
They said;

532
00:36:33,389 --> 00:36:34,972
تعادی بنا خیلنا

533
00:36:35,453 --> 00:36:42,058
They were on horseback and they reached to the place that Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

534
00:36:42,082 --> 00:36:45,519
you would find the woman, so they went up to this woman

535
00:36:45,867 --> 00:36:48,417
and they told her give us the letter that you have.

536
00:36:48,630 --> 00:36:50,083
She said: I don't have any letter.

537
00:36:50,460 --> 00:36:52,027
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told her.

538
00:36:52,273 --> 00:36:55,393
لَتُخْرِجِنَّ الكِتَابَ أَوْ لَنُلْقِيَنَّ الثِّيَابَ ،

539
00:36:55,820 --> 00:36:59,575
You either give us the letter or we would strip you from your clothes.

540
00:37:00,242 --> 00:37:01,346
We will strip search you.

541
00:37:01,700 --> 00:37:05,330
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ told us that you have a letter, that means you have a letter.

542
00:37:05,538 --> 00:37:10,808
She was lying, but they told her this is something that was told to us by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

543
00:37:10,832 --> 00:37:13,524
And if Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It, is the truth.

544
00:37:13,856 --> 00:37:20,088
So, either give us that letter, otherwise, we'll take off your clothes, and search for that letter.

545
00:37:20,365 --> 00:37:21,806
فَلَمَّا رأت أنهُ الجد

546
00:37:21,935 --> 00:37:26,696
So, when she saw that the matter is serious, she told them: Aarizoo(أعرضو), turn away

547
00:37:27,108 --> 00:37:34,235
and then she pulled out a letter from her hair, it was hidden in her hair.

548
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:38,997
She pulled out the letter and the letter was from Hatib Ibn Abi Baltaa(حاطب ابن اَبي بلتعة), one of the Sahabah(صحابه).

549
00:37:39,330 --> 00:37:44,912
He wrote a letter to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) informing them of the plans of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

550
00:37:45,365 --> 00:37:53,451
So, this thing that Hatib(حاطب) did, acting as an agent for the Kuffar(كفار) among the Muslims is a very dangerous thing.

551
00:37:53,681 --> 00:37:58,070
He's telling the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) about secret plans of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

552
00:37:59,054 --> 00:38:01,173
When Rasool Ullah saw the letter and he read it,

553
00:38:01,544 --> 00:38:04,533
he summoned Hatib Ibn Abi Baltaa(حاطب ابن اَبي بلتعة) and he told him;

554
00:38:04,558 --> 00:38:05,203
ما هذا؟

555
00:38:05,243 --> 00:38:06,283
What is this?

556
00:38:07,236 --> 00:38:10,071
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

557
00:38:10,365 --> 00:38:11,377
Hatib(حاطب) said;

558
00:38:11,692 --> 00:38:18,004
يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ، لَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيَّ،  إِنِّي كُنْتُ امْرَأً مُلْصقا فِيْ قُرَيْشٍ

559
00:38:18,562 --> 00:38:24,292
He said: O Rasool Ullah don't hurry in making a decision about me ٰ.

560
00:38:24,967 --> 00:38:26,387
I was a man not belonging to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

561
00:38:26,650 --> 00:38:30,035
مُلْصقا فِيْ قُرَيْشٍ ، يَقُوْلُ كُنْتُ حَلِيْفًا وَلَمْ أَكُنْ مِنْ أَنْفُسِهَا

562
00:38:30,164 --> 00:38:31,642
I did not belong to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

563
00:38:31,927 --> 00:38:38,873
وَكَانَ مَنْ مَعَكَ مِنَ المُهَاجِرِينَ مَن لَّهُمْ قَرَابَاتٌ يَحْمُونَ أَهْلِيهِمْ وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ

564
00:38:39,295 --> 00:38:46,657
فَأَحْبَبْتُ إِذْ فَاتَنِي ذَالِكَ مِنْ النَّسَبِ فِيهِمْ ، أَنْ أَتَخِذَ عِنْدَهُمْ يَدًا يَحْمُونَ بِهَا قَرَابَتِي

565
00:38:47,066 --> 00:38:56,213
He said: Your companions have families in Makkah, who would take care of their relative

566
00:38:56,281 --> 00:38:59,153
 because they belong to clans in Makkah.

567
00:38:59,446 --> 00:39:04,325
They have people who would take care of their families and take care of their wealth.

568
00:39:04,540 --> 00:39:08,829
But I do not have any relatives in Makkah, to take care of my family and my wealth.

569
00:39:09,255 --> 00:39:11,848
So, I wanted to do Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) a favor,

570
00:39:12,165 --> 00:39:16,946
so that they would protect or they would not harm my family.

571
00:39:16,971 --> 00:39:22,090
And in another narration it says; His mother was the one, who was living in Makkah

572
00:39:22,130 --> 00:39:24,756
and he was worried about her condition.

573
00:39:25,387 --> 00:39:29,691
I'll read you the translation of his words, Hatib(حاطب) said;

574
00:39:29,715 --> 00:39:33,500
O Allah's apostle do not make a hasty decision about me,

575
00:39:33,957 --> 00:39:36,179
I was a person not belonging to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

576
00:39:36,219 --> 00:39:41,506
but I was an ally to them, from outside and had no blood relation with them.

577
00:39:41,854 --> 00:39:46,711
And all the immigrants who were, with you have got, their kinsmen in Makkah,

578
00:39:47,113 --> 00:39:49,946
who can protect their families and properties.

579
00:39:50,333 --> 00:39:57,756
So, I liked to do them a favor, so that they might protect my relatives as I have no blood relation with them.

580
00:39:58,137 --> 00:40:01,715
 I did not do this to renegade from my religion

581
00:40:02,220 --> 00:40:07,114
nor did I do it to choose, heathenism after Islam.

582
00:40:07,860 --> 00:40:14,395
So, Hatib(حاطب) is making it clear that I didn't do this as Nifaq(نفاق) or apostasy

583
00:40:14,558 --> 00:40:19,024
In fact, he used the exact word Irtidadan(إرتدادًا), which is Riddah(ردة),

584
00:40:19,419 --> 00:40:21,068
ارْتِدَادًا عَنْ دِينِي

585
00:40:21,408 --> 00:40:23,499
Means I did not become an apostate.

586
00:40:24,003 --> 00:40:25,906
Now, this shows us

587
00:40:26,184 --> 00:40:28,507
because there is a difference of opinion among the Ulema(علماء)

588
00:40:28,547 --> 00:40:33,708
whether such an act is an act of Kuffr(كفر), or an act of Fisq(فسق).

589
00:40:34,080 --> 00:40:38,433
However, you can see here from what Hatib(حاطب) said is that

590
00:40:38,603 --> 00:40:42,643
he considers this act to be an act of Apostasy.

591
00:40:42,683 --> 00:40:45,648
And that's why he's saying I didn't commit apostasy.

592
00:40:45,893 --> 00:40:50,354
If he didn't consider this act to be an act of Kuffr(كفر), why would you say that?

593
00:40:50,609 --> 00:40:55,983
Because he saying that I did not commit Kuffr(كفر), I did not disbelieve.

594
00:40:56,414 --> 00:41:00,512
So, the fact that he is defending himself against apostasy,

595
00:41:01,134 --> 00:41:05,779
shows that he considered the act itself to be an act of Apostasy.

596
00:41:06,307 --> 00:41:10,404
However, his intentions were not intentions of kuffr(كفر).

597
00:41:11,017 --> 00:41:12,296
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

598
00:41:12,449 --> 00:41:13,621
اَمَا إِنَّهُ قَدْ صَدَقَكُمْ

599
00:41:13,652 --> 00:41:14,594
He's telling you the truth.

600
00:41:15,290 --> 00:41:16,582
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

601
00:41:16,695 --> 00:41:21,128
يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ دَعْنِي أَضْرِبَ عُنُقَهُ’ هَذَ الْمُنَافِقْ

602
00:41:21,843 --> 00:41:28,307
O Messenger of Allah, allow me to cut off the head of this Munafiq(منافق), this hypocrite,

603
00:41:28,859 --> 00:41:33,599
again, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) consider this act, to be an act of Nifaq(نفاق),

604
00:41:34,046 --> 00:41:37,561
an act of kuffr(كفر), and therefore he wanted to kill Hatib(حاطب).

605
00:41:37,987 --> 00:41:41,370
If he did not consider it to be an act of Riddah(ردة),

606
00:41:41,580 --> 00:41:46,404
why would he ask Rasool Allah ﷺ to allow him to kill Hatib(حاطب).

607
00:41:46,764 --> 00:41:48,851
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

608
00:41:49,066 --> 00:41:57,831
إِنَّهُ قد شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَمَا يُدْرِيكَ ؟ لَعَلَّ اللَّهَ اطَّلَعَ عَلَى مَنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا فَقَالَ : اعْمَلُوا مَا شِئْتُمْ فَقَدْ غَفَرْتُ لَكُمْ

609
00:41:58,081 --> 00:42:02,748
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: He has witnessed the Battle of Badr(بدر)

610
00:42:03,008 --> 00:42:09,090
and what could tell you, perhaps Allah looked at those, who witness Badr(بدر) and said;

611
00:42:09,282 --> 00:42:14,007
O the people of Badr(بدر) do what you like, for I have forgiven you.

612
00:42:14,786 --> 00:42:16,934
There are two things from the statement of Rasool Ullah,

613
00:42:16,958 --> 00:42:20,235
The first, it shows you the high status of the people of Badr(بدر).

614
00:42:21,053 --> 00:42:26,582
The second is that, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not disapprove what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said

615
00:42:26,781 --> 00:42:31,156
but he said: I mean, Rasool Ullah did not say that he does not deserve to be killed.

616
00:42:31,551 --> 00:42:37,259
Rasool Ullah did not respond to what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said, in regarding to the Nifaq(نفاق).

617
00:42:37,283 --> 00:42:38,880
But Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

618
00:42:39,077 --> 00:42:43,657
The reason why he should not be killed, is because he has witness Badr(بدر)

619
00:42:44,188 --> 00:42:49,121
which could also be an indication that Rasool Ullah approved the understanding of Umar(عُمَر),

620
00:42:49,626 --> 00:42:53,430
in accusing a person, who commits such an act of being a Munafiq(منافق),

621
00:42:53,629 --> 00:42:57,850
but because Hatib(حاطب) witnessed the Battle of Badr(بدر), he should not be punished for it.

622
00:42:58,284 --> 00:43:01,562
Again this shows us the high status of the people of Badr(بدر),

623
00:43:01,894 --> 00:43:07,324
and the great level that they have in the eyes of Rasool Allah ﷺ

624
00:43:07,758 --> 00:43:13,454
and even the angels because of Jibreel عليه السّلام, he came to Muhammadﷺ and said;

625
00:43:13,478 --> 00:43:16,243
What do you consider the people of Badr(بدر) to be among you?

626
00:43:16,338 --> 00:43:19,031
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We consider them to be among the best.

627
00:43:19,183 --> 00:43:23,648
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) said: And that is also with the angels who attended Badr(بدر).

628
00:43:23,941 --> 00:43:27,296
So, not only, are the people who attended Badr(بدر) the best,

629
00:43:27,320 --> 00:43:30,382
but also the angels who attended Badr(بدر) are the best.

630
00:43:30,406 --> 00:43:34,928
It is a battle that was witnessed by the creation of the heavens and the earth.

631
00:43:35,354 --> 00:43:37,444
And then Allahعزوجل revealed;

632
00:43:37,714 --> 00:43:51,205
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا عَدُوِّي وَعَدُوَّكُمْ أَوْلِيَاءَ تُلْقُونَ إِلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَوَدَّةِ وَقَدْ

633
00:43:51,575 --> 00:43:57,443
 وَقَدْ كَفَرُوا بِمَا جَاءَكُمْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ

634
00:43:57,821 --> 00:44:09,062
يُخْرِجُونَ الرَّسُولَ وَإِيَّاكُمْ أَنْ تُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ رَبِّكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ خَرَجْتُمْ جِهَادًا

635
00:44:09,538 --> 00:44:18,213
إِنْ كُنْتُمْ خَرَجْتُمْ جِهَادًا فِي سَبِيلِي وَابْتِغَاءَ مَرْضَاتِي

636
00:44:18,642 --> 00:44:28,448
تُسِرُّونَ إِلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَوَدَّةِ وَأَنَا أَعْلَمُ بِمَا أَخْفَيْتُمْ وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُمْ ۚ

637
00:44:28,840 --> 00:44:36,490
 وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْهُ مِنْكُمْ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَاءَ السَّبِيلِ۝

638
00:44:37,041 --> 00:44:39,743
The Ayaat(آيات) of Surat Ul Mumtahinna(سورة الممتحنه) were revealed.

639
00:44:40,060 --> 00:44:44,895
These Ayaat(آيات) are talking about this particular incident of Hatib Ibn Abi Balta(حاتب ابن ابي بلته)

640
00:44:44,935 --> 00:44:46,263
 and again this is in Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ).

641
00:44:46,549 --> 00:44:52,757
Allahعزوجل says: O you believe take not my enemies and your enemies as friends

642
00:44:53,127 --> 00:44:58,387
offering them your love, even though they have disbelieved in that truth

643
00:44:59,164 --> 00:45:04,346
which has come to you and who so ever, of you Muslims does that

644
00:45:04,370 --> 00:45:07,934
then indeed he has gone far astray away from the straight path.

645
00:45:08,576 --> 00:45:17,281
So, to all those Muslims, who allowed themselves to work as agents, with the kuffar(كفار)

646
00:45:17,488 --> 00:45:23,806
spying on the Muslims conveying information about the Muslims to the disbelievers,

647
00:45:24,047 --> 00:45:28,069
they have committed an act of Apostasy, they are Munafiqeen(منافقين).

648
00:45:28,230 --> 00:45:30,128
It is a very dangerous sin,

649
00:45:30,452 --> 00:45:35,912
 it is a very dangerous thing to spy for the disbelievers against the Muslims.

650
00:45:36,310 --> 00:45:40,556
And one of the ironies of our age is that

651
00:45:40,651 --> 00:45:50,355
in some Masajid(مساجد) intelligence agencies were given a booth to recruit from the Musalleen(مصلين)

652
00:45:50,500 --> 00:45:52,691
to work as spies against the Muslims.

653
00:45:53,586 --> 00:45:59,656
That's one of the most amazing things that happened in our age and time.

654
00:46:00,184 --> 00:46:01,950
These are Masajid(مساجد) of Zaraar(ضرار),

655
00:46:02,072 --> 00:46:06,330
and we will talk about the Masjid(مسجد) of Zarrar(مسجد), when we talk about the Battle of Tabook(تبوك).

656
00:46:06,998 --> 00:46:12,091
Regarding the Hukum(حكم) of Al-Jasoos(ألجاسوس), the spy who spies against the Muslims.

657
00:46:12,399 --> 00:46:17,021
The Fuqahaa(فقهاء), the scholars of Islam have a consensus

658
00:46:17,440 --> 00:46:22,953
that the disbelieving spy is killed.

659
00:46:23,184 --> 00:46:26,033
Then there is a difference of opinion regarding the zimmi(ضمي),

660
00:46:26,389 --> 00:46:29,737
the zimmi(ضمي) is the Christian or the Jew, who's paying Jizyah(جزيه).

661
00:46:30,179 --> 00:46:32,940
According to the Ahnaaf(أحناف), their opinion

662
00:46:33,035 --> 00:46:34,767
يُوْجَع وَيُحْبَسْ وَلَا يُقْتَلْ

663
00:46:35,317 --> 00:46:38,654
That he should be physically harmed Ya'ani(يعني) painful harm

664
00:46:39,114 --> 00:46:42,117
and he should be imprisoned, but he should not be killed.

665
00:46:42,142 --> 00:46:43,830
This is the opinion of Ahnaaf(أحناف).

666
00:46:44,335 --> 00:46:46,415
 The Shafiyah(شافيه) have a difference of opinion.

667
00:46:46,660 --> 00:46:49,272
While Malik(مالك) and Al-Aozaee(أوذاعي) say;

668
00:46:49,551 --> 00:46:54,433
That this is a breach of their covenant with the Muslims and therefore they should be killed.

669
00:46:54,914 --> 00:46:59,106
Regarding the Muslim, the Hanafiyah(حنفيه) and Shafiyah(شافيه) and Hanabila(حنابله)

670
00:46:59,392 --> 00:47:01,601
they say that he should be punished but not killed.

671
00:47:02,106 --> 00:47:03,353
While Al-Malikia(مالكيه) say;

672
00:47:03,377 --> 00:47:07,443
يَجْتَهِدْ فِيْ الْاِمَامْ وَلَه’ قَتْلُه’ وَمَالَ اِلی ذَالِكْ اِبْنِ الْقَيِّمْ

673
00:47:07,595 --> 00:47:09,601
The Maliki(مالكي) scholars say;

674
00:47:09,864 --> 00:47:15,646
That the Imam(اِمَام) has a right to do with such a person whatever he sees the Masliha(مصلحه),

675
00:47:15,686 --> 00:47:18,944
whichever he sees is better, and he can kill him, if he wants to.

676
00:47:19,339 --> 00:47:21,613
And this is also the opinion of Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبن القيم).

677
00:47:22,461 --> 00:47:27,577
Rasool Allah ﷺ march forth in the month of Ramadan(رمضان).

678
00:47:28,246 --> 00:47:31,721
And in the initial parts of the journey they were fasting

679
00:47:31,975 --> 00:47:38,130
but when they were getting closer to Makkah Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered the Muslims to break their fast

680
00:47:38,507 --> 00:47:43,513
and he took a cup of water and he drank it, in front of them, to give them the example.

681
00:47:43,946 --> 00:47:46,888
And the army was 10,000 strong.

682
00:47:47,807 --> 00:47:52,220
This was the largest army assembled by Rasool Allah ﷺ so far.

683
00:47:52,666 --> 00:47:56,313
All of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and all of the Ansaar(أنصار) were included

684
00:47:56,645 --> 00:48:00,852
And many of the tribes surrounding Madina participated such as

685
00:48:00,920 --> 00:48:05,452
Sulaim(سليم) and Aslam(أسلم) and Ghifaar(غفار) and Muzaina(مضينه)

686
00:48:05,745 --> 00:48:12,216
all of these tribes they participated and that's why we have this large number of 10,000 strong.

687
00:48:12,671 --> 00:48:20,172
And these are the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, who witnessed the great battle of Fatiha Makkah(فتح مكه).

688
00:48:21,363 --> 00:48:28,725
We'll continue In Sha Allah-Ho-Ta'ala(إن شاءالله تعالى) with the rest of Fatiha Makkah(فتح مكه) in our next session.

689
00:48:29,176 --> 00:48:33,292
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًاكَثِيْرَا

